<figure class="accessible-modal-anatomy" aria-labelledby="accessible-modal-caption">
  <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__layout">
    <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__scene" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__page">
        <span>Account settings</span>
        <i></i>
        <b>Open settings</b>
      </div>
      <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__backdrop"></div>
      <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__dialog">
        <header><strong>Settings</strong><span>Close</span></header>
        <p>Manage your account preferences.</p>
        <div class="accessible-modal-anatomy__field"></div>
        <footer><b>Cancel</b><b>Save changes</b></footer>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Name the dialog</strong><p>Give it an accessible label and modal semantics.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Keep focus inside</strong><p>Tab should cycle through the dialog, not the page behind it.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Handle dismissal</strong><p>Support Escape and a clear close control.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Restore the trigger</strong><p>Return focus to the button that opened the dialog.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="accessible-modal-caption">A portal gives the dialog a safe place to render. It does not provide the focus and keyboard behavior that make a modal accessible.</figcaption>
</figure>

